- It terminates the process when it leaves the DNA at a termination site.

2. DNA polymerase in replication: DNA polymerase is responsible for synthesizing a new DNA strand from an existing DNA template. The process of replication is the process of copying the entire DNA sequence to create a new copy of the DNA. The role of DNA polymerase in this process is as follows:

