The mTOR inhibitors work through the following mechanism:  
1. **Dysregulation of the PI3K/AKT/mTOR Pathway**: In various malignancies, this pathway is dysregulated, leading to uncontrolled cell growth, proliferation, motility, and survival. It can also become constitutively activated as a resistance mechanism.  
