The y-intercept of a line or function is the value of \( y \) when \( x = 0 \). Substituting \( x = 0 \) into the equation \( y = \frac{1}{4} \cdot 4^x - 1 \):
\[
y = \frac{1}{4} \cdot 4^0 - 1
\]
Since \( 4^0 = 1 \), the equation becomes:
\[
y = \frac{1}{4} \cdot 1 - 1 = \frac{1}{4} - 1 = 0.25 - 1 = -0.75
\]
