   - After the collision, the initial velocity \( v_0 \) of mass \( m \) is conserved in the horizontal direction.  
   - The final velocities of the two objects after the collision are:  
     \[
     v_{1f} = e \cdot u_0 \quad \text{(for mass } m \text{)}
     \]  
     \[
     v_{2f} = u_0 \text{ (for mass } M \text{)}
     \]  
     where \( u_0 \) is the initial velocity of mass \( M \).  

