<USER_REQUEST>
What is the decay length of the evanescent wave in a GaAs core and Ga\(_{0.2}\)Al\(_{0.8}\)As cladding, where \(n_{\text{eff}} - n_f \sim 0.3\), for a wavelength of 1 μm?
</USER_REQUEST>

<ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>
The decay length of an evanescent wave is given by:  
\[
\frac{1}{n_{\text{eff}} - n_{\text{film}}}
\]  
where \(n_{\text{eff}}\) is the effective index of the wafer, and \(n_{\text{film}}\) is the refractive index of the film.  

Given \(n_{\text{eff}} - n_f \sim 0.3\) and \(n_{\text{film}} = 1.09\) (for Si), the decay length is:  
\[
\frac{1}{0.3} \approx 3.3 \text{ μm}
\]  

Thus, the decay length is \(\boxed{3.3 \text{ μm}}\).
</ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>

