\[
R = \frac{1 - \omega \nu_0}{1 + \omega \nu_0}
\]
where \(\omega\) is the frequency of the incident light and \(\nu_0\) is the frequency of the emitted radiation. This is given by:
\[
\nu_0 = \frac{A}{B}
\]
Substituting \(\nu_0\) into the relation for \(R\):
\[
R = \frac{1 - \omega \frac{A}{B}}{1 + \omega \frac{A}{B}} = \frac{B - \omega A}{B + \omega A}
\]
This is the refractive index \(R\) of the system. 

